Jesus rules the Nafirim and the people of the Torah.
Jesus spoke to the crowds and to his disciples.
He said: "Evil scholars and musicians sit in the seat of Moses."
Well, you must obey them. Do everything they tell you to do. But don't do what they do. They don't practice what they preach.
They load burdens and place them on the shoulders of others. But they themselves do not wish to extend a finger to move them.
All that they do, they do to make people know it. And on their heads and their arms they put small boxes containing texts of the Holy Book. And they make these boxes very broad. And they make the feathers on the robes of some of them very long.
They love to sit in the place of honor at meals. They also love to get the reserved pews in churches that are considered the most important.
They like to be welcomed in the souqs. They like it when people call them "Rabbi".
But you should not be called "master". You are nothing but one servant, and you are all brothers.
Do not call anyone on earth 'father.' You have one Father, and He is in heaven.
You should not be called "Teacher." You have one Teacher, the Christ.
The most important person among you will be your servant.
He who exalts himself shall be abased, and he who is abased shall be exalted.
How terrible it will be for you, teachers of the law and you pharisees! You frauds! You block up the kingdom of heaven; you do not enter yourselves, nor do you allow those who want to enter to do so.
Please
What a tragedy for you, you breeders from the masters of Israel, and how you are forgers! You travel everywhere for Qatada, one man, then you make him double in hell. You are nothing but like him.
What a tragedy for you, blind guides! You say, "To take an oath in the name of the Temple is nothing. But to take an oath in the name of the gold of the Temple is binding."
You are blind and treacherous! Which is more important? Is it the gold? Or is it the temple which makes the gold sacred?
It also says: "Whoever joins the rank having taken something, has no right to it. As for whoever joins the gift having taken an oath, let him do what he swore."
Blind guides! Which is more important? Is it the offering? Or is it the altar that makes the offering sacred?
So then, whoever swears by the altar, swears by it and by everything on it.
And everyone who swore by the name of the temple, swore by it and by the Creator who dwelt in it.
And every one who swears by heaven, swears by the throne of God and by the intercessor who sits upon it.
What a tragedy for you, you breeders, you scholars of the Jews and the Persians! You pretenders! You give God sores from your spices, like mint, cumin, and mustard. But you have not practiced the most important matters of the Law, like justice, mercy, and faith. You should have practiced the latter matters without failing to do the former.
You blind guides! You filter out a gnat from your drink, and you swallow a camel whole!
Oh, what tragedies for you, you teachers, you scholars of the Jewish and Persian rabbis! You, who claim righteousness! You, who wash the outside of the dishes. But inside, you are full of greed. And you only want to satisfy yourselves.
You ignorant person! First, wash what is inside the cup and the pot, and then the outside will also become clean.
What a tragedy for you, you guardians and judges! You self-righteous people! You are like whitewashed tombs. They look beautiful on the outside, but on the inside they are full of the tombs of the dead. So also are they full of all manner of unclean and unholy things.
It is so with you also. From without you appear to be doing right, but within you are full of wrong. And you pretend that you are not what you are.
Oh, what calamities for you, you breeders and Vasileonists! You pretenders! You who build the tombs of the prophets. You who adorn the tombs of the righteous.
And you say, "If we had been in the time of our forefathers, we would not have done what they did. We would not have participated in the killing of the prophets."
You bear witness against yourselves. You have acknowledged that you are the sons of those who killed the bearers of the message.
