He replied with a text message: "Take some of the guards with you." "Go. Make the grave as secure as you can."
So they went to make the cemetery safe. They placed a seal on the rock and began assigning guards.
Jesus rose from the dead.
Saturday had ended. And the dawn had come on the first day of the week. Mary Magdalene and Joanna, and Salome, had come to see the tomb.
A great earthquake happened. The Angel of the Lord descended from Heaven. The Angel went to the tomb. He pushed the stone lid and sat on it.
His body shone like a lyre. His clothes were as white as snow.
The guards were trembling and looked like dead men, so afraid were they for him.
The angel said to the women, "Do not be afraid. I know that you are looking for Jesus, who was crucified."
He's not here! He has awakened, as he said he would awaken! Come see the place where he was.
Hurry! And tell his disciples, "Say: 'He has risen from the dead. He is going ahead of you to Galilea, where you will see him.' ' I have told you this."
The women ascended, seeking refuge from the cemetery. They were fearful, yet filled with joy. Then they rode to inform the messengers.
Suddenly, Jesus met them. He said, "Peace be with you!" They came to him and touched his feet and worshipped him.
Then Jesus said to them, "Do not be afraid. Go and tell my brothers to go to Galilee, where they will find me." The guards reported these words to the chief priests.
While the women were on their way, some of the guards entered the city. They reported to the chief priests everything that had happened.
When the chief priests and elders met together, they made a plan. And they gave a large sum of money to the soldiers.
They told the soldiers: "I want you to say: 'His disciples came at night. They stole his body while we were sleeping.'"
If the ruler hears this report, we will gift him. This will keep you out of trouble.
The soldiers took the money and did as they were told. This story spread all over among the Jews to this day. Jesus' last command to his apostles.
Then the twelve disciples went to Galilee. They went to the mountain to which Christ had told them to go.
When they saw him, they worshipped him. But some still had doubts.
