Therefore, hold fast and make disciples of all the nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit.
Teach them to obey everything I have commanded you. And be sure of this: I am with you always, even to the end of the age.
John the Baptist is preparing the way.
This is the beginning of the gospel of Jesus Christ, the Son of God.
A long time ago, Isaiah the prophet wrote: "I will send my messenger to prepare the way before you, and the Lord will make his glorious name known to his people Israel. I will come quickly to save you; I will take great delight in you, I will sing praises to you, declares the Lord." (Malachi 3:1)
A messenger cries out in the desert: "Prepare the way for your Lord. Make for him straight paths."
And so John came. And he baptized people in the desert. And he also called them to repentance and to follow from sins. Then God would forgive them.
All the people of the region of Galilee came to him. And all the people of Jerusalem went out to him also. And when they confessed their sins to him, he baptized them in the river Jordan.
John wore clothes made of sheep's wool. He wore a leather belt around his waist. He ate cockroach worms and wild honey.
This is what John used to preach. "After me will come one more powerful than I. I am not worthy to stoop down and untie his sandals."
I baptize you with water. But he will baptize you with the Holy Spirit. Jesus baptizes and tests.
At that time Jesus came from Nazareth in Galilee. And John was not yet cast into prison in the river Jordan.
