A voice called to him from heaven. It said, "You are my son, whom I love. I am very pleased with you."
Suddenly, the Holy Spirit sent Jesus into the desert.
He was in the desert for forty days. He was tempted by demons. The beasts did not harm Jesus. The angels submitted to him. Jesus chose the first apostles.
After Jesus put John in prison, he went to Gethsemane. And he came to preach the Gospel of God.
The time has come, he said. "The Kingdom of God is near. Shake off your sins and believe in the good experience!"
One day, Jesus was walking along the shore of Lake Galilee. There he saw Simon and his brother James. They were mending their fishing nets in the lake. They were fishermen.
Come, follow me, Jesus said. "I will make you fish for people."
So they went out in a group, among them the Shabakah, and they followed him.
Then Jesus went a little way further. And as he walked, he saw Simon the son of John, and his brother Andrew. And they were in a boat mending their nets.
Suddenly he fluttered and cried out to them. They left their father Zebedee in the boat mending nets with the hired men. Then they followed Jesus. Jesus was filled with the Holy Spirit of wickedness and adultery.
Jesus and His disciples went to Capernaum. And when the Sabbath day came, He entered the synagogue. And there He began to teach.
The ignorant were impressed by his phrases. He taught them like a prince, never deviating from the rule of scholars.
But suddenly, a man from their temple screamed. He was enchanted by an evil spirit. He said,
What do you want from us, Jesus Christ? Have you come to destroy us? I know who you are. You are God's Victorious One!
Be quiet! Jesus said firmly. "Come out of him!"
The evil spirit violently shook the man. Then it came out of him, crying out.
Everyone was astonished. They took comfort in one another, asking, "What is this? A new teaching! And with a strong command! Indeed, it commands the evil spirits, and they obey it."
News of Jesus spread quickly throughout Galilee. Jesus healed many people.
