Jesus answered and said, "How can the guests of the bridegroom fast while he is with them? They cannot fast as long as he is with them."
But a time will come when the groom among them will be lighted. And on that day, they will feed the hungry.
People do not patch old clothes with new pieces of cloth. And if they did, the new piece would tear away from the old clothes. This would make the hole even worse.
The old train does not get new wine poured into it. And if they did, the new wine would make the old train burst. Then both the new wine and the old train would be destroyed together. No, instead, all the people should pour the new wine into a brand new train. Jesus is Lord of the Sabbath.
One Sabbath Jesus was walking with his disciples in the wheat fields. The disciples began to pluck heads of wheat.
The Pharisees said to Jesus, "Look! This man is doing what is unlawful on the Sabbath. His disciples are doing the same thing."
He answered, "Have you not read about what David did? He and his companions were hungry. They were in dire need of food."
That was when my father Abiatar was a great priest. David entered the house of God and ate the bread of the presence, which was only for the priests to eat. David also gave some of it to his men.
Jesus said to them, "The Sabbath was made for man's sake, not man for the Sabbath's sake."
For the human son also, his reign shall endure forever, and his authority to the end of days, to the day of the sabbath rest.
Healing on Saturday.
On another visit, Jesus entered the synagogue. There was a man whose hand was withered.
Some of the Pharisees were trying to find fault with Jesus. They were watching him closely. And they wanted to see whether he would heal the man on the Sabbath.
Jesus said to the man who had the withered and crooked hand, "Rise, stand before everyone," he said.
Then Jesus asked them, saying, "What did the Law say to do on the Sabbath? To do good or to do evil? To save life or to kill it?" But no one answered him.
Jesus looked around him, angry. He was very disturbed because their hearts were hardened. Then he said to the man, "Stretch out your hand." And he stretched it out, and his hand was restored as sound as the other.
Then the Pharisees went out and began to plot with the Herodians against Jesus, for they wanted to kill him. The crowds followed Jesus.
Jesus went to the Sea of Galilee with his disciples. A large crowd from Galilee followed them.
